<!-- ───────────── What this is ───────────── -->
<section id="what">
  <div class="section-eyebrow">What this is</div>
  <h2>A productized ERP. <span class="accent">Ready to ship.</span></h2>
  <p class="section-lede">Built by OneDigital, now an HSO portfolio asset. The codebase, the integrations, and the runway — all transferred. This page is the entry point for everyone who needs to understand it.</p>

  <div class="pillars">
    <a class="pillar" href="hub-cash-hub.html">
      <div class="pillar-num">01</div>
      <h4>Cash Hub</h4>
      <p>Statement ingestion with AI mapping, cash application, journals, accruals, collections.</p>
      <div class="pillar-link-cue">Open the Cash Hub overview →</div>
    </a>
    <a class="pillar" href="hub-comp-hub.html">
      <div class="pillar-num">02</div>
      <h4>Compensation Hub</h4>
      <p>Producer comp rules, split intake with versioning, payable transactions, user security.</p>
      <div class="pillar-link-cue">Open the Compensation Hub overview →</div>
    </a>
    <a class="pillar" href="hub-producer-portal.html">
      <div class="pillar-num">03</div>
      <h4>Producer Portal</h4>
      <p>External-facing self-service for producers and brokers. Dual-OIDC authentication.</p>
      <div class="pillar-link-cue">Open the Producer Portal overview →</div>
    </a>
    <a class="pillar" href="hub-integration-hub.html">
      <div class="pillar-num">04</div>
      <h4>Integration Hub</h4>
      <p>Six Azure Function apps wiring it to Accounting Hub, FinOps, Workday, Mulesoft, and more.</p>
      <div class="pillar-link-cue">Open the Integration Hub overview →</div>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────── Learning packs ───────────── -->
<section id="packs">
  <div class="section-eyebrow">Learning packs</div>
  <h2>Pick your <span class="accent">role.</span></h2>
  <p class="section-lede">Five audience-specific learning packs, each in HSO brand. PowerPoint for email and SharePoint; HTML for native browser viewing.</p>

  <div class="audience-grid" id="audience-grid">

    <div class="card executive">
      <div class="card-icon">E</div>
      <h3>Executive Overview</h3>
      <div class="card-role">CXO · Board · Portfolio leadership</div>
      <p class="card-desc">What ERP Unite is, why it matters, and what HSO is bringing to market — built for OneDigital, productized for the industry. Sixteen slides. Confident. No jargon.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span><strong>16</strong> slides</span><span><strong>~6</strong> min read</span></div>
      <div class="card-links">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="01-executive-overview.html">View</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="01-executive-overview.pptx">⬇ PPTX</a>
        <a class="btn btn-watch" href="01-executive-overview.mp4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">▶ Watch</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card sales">
      <div class="card-icon">S</div>
      <h3>Sales Enablement</h3>
      <div class="card-role">HSO sellers · Account executives</div>
      <p class="card-desc">The playbook: buyer personas, three customer pains, competitive positioning, twenty-minute demo path, top three objections.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span><strong>18</strong> slides</span><span><strong>~8</strong> min read</span></div>
      <div class="card-links">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="02-sales-enablement.html">View</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="02-sales-enablement.pptx">⬇ PPTX</a>
        <a class="btn btn-watch" href="02-sales-enablement.mp4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">▶ Watch</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card functional">
      <div class="card-icon">F</div>
      <h3>Functional Consultant</h3>
      <div class="card-role">Implementation · Business analysts</div>
      <p class="card-desc">Five end-to-end business flows. Configuration touchpoints. Statement &rarr; cash &rarr; GL &rarr; accrual &rarr; collections, with every screen named.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span><strong>26</strong> slides</span><span><strong>~13</strong> min read</span></div>
      <div class="card-links">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="03-functional-consultant.html">View</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="03-functional-consultant.pptx">⬇ PPTX</a>
        <a class="btn btn-watch" href="03-functional-consultant.mp4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">▶ Watch</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card technical">
      <div class="card-icon">T</div>
      <h3>Technical Architect</h3>
      <div class="card-role">Developers · Tech leads · DevOps</div>
      <p class="card-desc">CQRS without MediatR, EF Core + Unit of Work, the handoff/polling pattern, authorization model, six function apps, AI integration.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span><strong>21</strong> slides</span><span><strong>~15</strong> min read</span></div>
      <div class="card-links">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="04-technical-architect.html">View</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="04-technical-architect.pptx">⬇ PPTX</a>
        <a class="btn btn-watch" href="04-technical-architect.mp4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">▶ Watch</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card ea">
      <div class="card-icon">EA</div>
      <h3>Enterprise Architect</h3>
      <div class="card-role">EA office · Portfolio strategy</div>
      <p class="card-desc">Where this fits in HSO's portfolio, business capabilities delivered, value flow through the customer ecosystem, cohabitation with existing tech, vendor + risk posture, investment trajectory.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span><strong>22</strong> slides</span><span><strong>~13</strong> min read</span></div>
      <div class="card-links">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="05-enterprise-architect.html">View</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="05-enterprise-architect.pptx">⬇ PPTX</a>
        <a class="btn btn-watch" href="05-enterprise-architect.mp4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">▶ Watch</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card pm">
      <div class="card-icon">PM</div>
      <h3>Project Manager</h3>
      <div class="card-role">PMs leading customer conversations</div>
      <p class="card-desc">Product literacy in a single sitting. The one-paragraph elevator pitch, the four moving parts, the five business flows, twenty terms of vocabulary, the customer Q&amp;A shortlist, and escalation cues for when to call a functional consultant.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span><strong>20</strong> slides</span><span><strong>~11</strong> min read</span></div>
      <div class="card-links">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="07-project-manager.html">View</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="07-project-manager.pptx">⬇ PPTX</a>
        <a class="btn btn-watch" href="07-project-manager.mp4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">▶ Watch</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-icon" style="background: var(--slate);">D</div>
      <h3>Reference Material</h3>
      <div class="card-role">For everyone</div>
      <p class="card-desc">The feature library (25 narrative guides, prev/next navigable), the architecture guide, the productization spec, and the split-feature reference spec. HSO-themed HTML throughout.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span><strong>25</strong> feature guides</span><span><strong>+ 3</strong> spec docs</span></div>
      <div class="card-links">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="feature-library.html">Feature Library</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="architecture.html">Architecture</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="productization.html">Productization</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="split-feature-spec.html">Split Feature Spec</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="border-top-color: transparent;">
      <div class="card-icon" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--cyan) 0%, var(--teal) 100%);">📚</div>
      <h3>Screens Library</h3>
      <div class="card-role">Self-guided product tour · 51 screens</div>
      <p class="card-desc">Every screen in ERP Unite — top-level pages plus all 6 StatementDetails tabs (Dashboard, Lines, Review, Unmatched, Review &amp; Approve) — with a learning guide behind each tile. What it does, where the data comes from, vocabulary, customer Q&amp;A. Pages flagged as &quot;needs data&quot; are explicitly noted.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span><strong>51</strong> screen guides</span><span><strong>3</strong> need data</span></div>
      <div class="card-links">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="screens-library.html">Open library</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="screen-cashhub-mapping-studio.html">Mapping Studio</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="screen-comphub-split-intake-list-all.html">Split Intake</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

